  "notes": "Release date printed on page: 2026-03-18 (OpenRouter listing agrees; HuggingFace MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7 createdAt 2026-04-09 is the later open-weights upload - page date is authoritative, discrepancy recorded). Page is JS-rendered news post (web reader returns shell; headless browser used). All benchmark scores appear as prose claims - no DOM benchmark table, no benchmark images; rows are prose-verified. Page spells one benchmark 'Toolathon' with the value 46.3 which matches GLM-5.1's Tool-Decathlon column for M2.7 - recorded under tool-decathlon with the spelling discrepancy noted. Self-evolution workflow disclosed: internal M2.7 built its own research-agent harness; M2.7 autonomously optimized a model's programming performance over 100+ iterative rounds (analyze -> plan -> modify -> evaluate -> keep/revert), achieving 30% improvement on internal eval sets; handled 30%-50% of the RL team's daily workflow. MLE-Bench Lite exploration: 22 OpenAI open-sourced competitions on single A30 GPUs, 3 trials x 24h, best run 9 gold / 5 silver / 1 bronze; average medal rate 66.6% (second to Opus-4.6 75.7% and GPT-5.4 71.2%, tying Gemini-3.1 66.6%). Production debugging: live incident recovery reduced to under three minutes on multiple occasions (qualitative)."
